      "content": "The UN has been a fundamental failure in preventing major conflicts throughout the 21st century, as its reliance on the veto power of permanent members has repeatedly paralyzed it during crises like the war in Ukraine and the conflict in Gaza. Instead of acting as a global peacekeeper, the organization often serves as a tool for geopolitical manipulation, allowing powerful nations to shield their own aggression while condemning their adversaries. This structural flaw has allowed major wars to escalate unchecked, proving that the current international framework is incapable of enforcing true global security without significant reform.",
      "source": "target",
